{
  "id": "nyu-elegant",
  "name": "NYU Elegant",
  "aiInstructions": "Audience: NYU students, faculty and staff from any school — educated generalists, not specialists in this subject. Write plain, precise academic English. Expand an acronym the first time it appears and define a term of art the first time it is used. Prefer a concrete example to an abstraction. Sentence case for titles and bullets; no full stop at the end of a bullet. One idea per slide. No hype, no emoji, no exclamation marks. State the point outright rather than teasing it. Name the source in the caption for any quotation, figure or statistic that is not the lecturer's own.",
  "theme": {
    "background": "#ffffff",
    "surface": "#f3f3f3",
    "text": "#333333",
    "muted": "#9a6aba",
    "accent": "#57068c",
